# Authoritative project documentation

The following files in `docs/` are the **single source of truth** for this project.
Read the relevant one(s) BEFORE any task that touches game logic, scripts, or systems.

| File | Read before working on |
|------|------------------------|
| `docs/CRITICAL CODING & COMMUNICATION RULES.txt` | Every task — coding/communication rules |
| `docs/GAME DESIGN REFERENCE - Port Design.txt` | Gameplay, levels, characters, camera, devices, environment |
| `docs/POWER SYSTEM TECHNICAL REFERENCE 3.0.txt` | Anything touching Power Source, Runode, RunodeFace, Line Port, Obstruction Port, MW, propagation, circuits |

## Non-authoritative (ignore unless user says otherwise)
- `AGENTS.md` — autogenerated, do not treat as source of truth
- `SETUP.md` — autogenerated setup checklist
- `.cursor/rules/project-context.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/unity-csharp.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/power-system.mdc` — autogenerated, superseded by the docs above

## How to use the docs
- When a task touches the power system, read `POWER SYSTEM TECHNICAL REFERENCE 3.0.txt` end-to-end first.
- When a task touches gameplay/level design, read `GAME DESIGN REFERENCE - Port Design.txt`.
- Always follow `CRITICAL CODING & COMMUNICATION RULES.txt` — minimal diffs, ask when unclear, no out-of-scope changes, no code in Ask mode, root-cause debugging.
- If the docs and the code disagree, ask the user which is correct before changing either.
